# Local scaffolding and private corpora — never publish or vendor into this repo.
# These names are ALREADY public in this repo's history (.gitignore and scripts/check.sh on main),
# so withholding them here protects nothing and removing them only deletes a working guard.
# Add your own private directories here AND to local/private-pattern.txt, so both the path-level
# guard (this file) and the content-level gate (scripts/check.sh) cover them.
research/
BAD_GUIDE.md
researchfms/
guidesfm/
local/
.claude/

# `research/` is the line that matters most and the one an earlier pass in this very session
# dropped while restoring the other four. It holds a LIVE API key and ~177 MB of private corpus,
# none of it in any commit — so removing this line would have been FIRST-TIME credential exposure,
# not a re-leak. Four reviewers checked the diff and none caught it; the content-level gate below
# reported 0 failures throughout, because an unignored directory at the repo root is not file
# content under any path it scans. scripts/check.sh now has a path-level pass for exactly this.
